  "body": "## What this PR does\n\nThis PR adds the new crate `crates/gcode` (`camcraft-gcode`). The crate reads RS-274/NGC and ISO 6983 3-axis milling programs. It gives `cl::Toolpath` sections and a 1-based line map. It refuses unsupported words by name and line number.\n\n- The crate depends on `camcraft-cl`, `camcraft-geometry` and `thiserror` only.\n- It decodes the modal groups, `I`/`J`/`K` and `R` arcs in `G17`/`G18`/`G19`, and the canned cycles `G73`, `G81`, `G82`, `G83`, `G84`, `G85`, `G86`, `G89` with `G98`/`G99` and `L`.\n- It splits sections at `T`/`M6`. It reads `S`, `M3`-`M5`, `M0`-`M2`, `M30`, `G4`, `G61`, `G64`, `G53`, `G28` and `G30`.\n- It refuses `G41`/`G42`, macros (`G65`, `M98`, `#`), probing (`G31`, `G38.2`), `R` full circles, a missing `G20`/`G21`, a missing reference position, and `A`/`B`/`C`.\n\nSources: RS-274/NGC (NISTIR 6556), ISO 6983, and the public controller documents that `crates/gcode/src/dialect.rs` names for the dwell and arc presets. No other parser code was used.\n\n## Held work\n\n- Commit `711314efd` by Mike Kinney, from `mkinney:issue/2217-camcraft-gcode`. It has the crate, its 9 tests, the decision file and the gate plan entries.\n- This PR keeps that commit and its author unchanged. A merge commit (`db23cf9bd`) joins it to main `60376ccbb`.\n\n## Added after the held commit\n\n- `db23cf9bd` merge: the conflict resolution (next section).\n- `75b33ace3` `test(xtask)`: two xtask tests of main list the crates by hand. `heavy_plan_tests::reach_follows_the_crate_dependencies` now expects `gcode` in the reach of `geometry`. `step_tests::batch_prebuild_leaves_suite_steps_fresh_with_truck_dev_dep` now writes a stub `crates/gcode`. `Cargo.lock` takes the version `0.25.0` for `camcraft-gcode`.\n- `92627aef0` `test(gcode)`:\n  - Each gcode suite has a `Gate map: covers camcraft_gcode::{..}` line. Quick then selects the suites for a change in each `crates/gcode/src` module.\n  - The new suite `degenerate_input` checks malformed programs. Each one gives a value or a refusal, with no panic and no hang.\n  - The decision file records the merge.\n\n## Conflict resolution\n\nAll three conflicts were lists. No logic hunk had a conflict.\n\n- Root `Cargo.toml`: the `members` line has main's `\"crates/gpu\"` and the held `\"crates/gcode\"` (after `\"crates/cl\"`). The `camcraft-gcode` workspace dependency merged without a conflict.\n- `xtask/src/plan.rs`: `BATCH_CRATES`, `ALL_CRATES` and `CLIPPY` have `\"gcode\"` after `\"cl\"` and main's `\"gpu\"` after `\"app\"`.\n- `xtask/src/tests.rs`: the release step count keeps main's known-fail `checks` term. It uses the held `plan::ALL_CRATES.len()` in place of the fixed `10`.\n- `Cargo.lock` merged without a conflict.\n\n## New crate edges\n\n- `camcraft-gcode -> camcraft-cl`: `ArcPlane`, `Cycle`, `CycleKind`, `MoveKind`, `PathBuilder`, `Toolpath`, `lattice`.\n- `camcraft-gcode -> camcraft-geometry`: `geo2d::Point2`, `Point3`, `units::{from_display, Unit, MM_PER_INCH}`.\n- `docs/decisions/2217-camcraft-gcode.md` gives the imported items, the reason that a caller cannot pass the values in, and the rebuild impact. No crate depends on `camcraft-gcode` yet.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `gcode_3axis`:\n  - `modal_groups_track_and_sections_split_on_tool_changes`\n  - `ijk_and_r_arcs_xy_xz_yz_and_full_circle`\n  - `r_major_vs_minor_arc_centers_differ_as_expected`\n  - `canned_cycles_expand_into_move_chains_and_honor_g98_g99`\n  - `unit_scaling_g20_inches_to_mm_and_unscaled_s_t_p`\n  - `reference_moves_g53_g28_g30_execute_when_configured_and_refuse_when_missing`\n  - `unsupported_codes_and_bad_inputs_refuse_by_name_with_line_number`\n- `dialects_and_planes`:\n  - `vertical_plane_r_arcs_xz_and_yz_minor_and_major`\n  - `dialects_dwell_units_ream_and_m6_tool_order`\n- `degenerate_input` (new): `degenerate_programs_refuse_or_parse_without_panic_or_hang`\n\n## Gate\n\nAll results are on head `92627aef0`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: the batch plan, because `Cargo.lock` changed. Result: 1133 steps, 1 failed, 0 stalled. The failed step is `clippy -D warnings` in `camcraft-gpu`. See \"Known red step\".\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gcode --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass, 0 warnings.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-gcode`:\n  - `gcode_3axis`: 7 passed.\n  - `dialects_and_planes`: 2 passed.\n  - `degenerate_input`: 1 passed.\n  - 0 failed.\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 295 passed in the lib test binary. The 6 other test binaries passed. 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 3 steps, 0 failed.\n- Full heavy lanes: not run. The rule of #3556 keeps them for the cut.\n\n## Known red step\n\nThe failed quick step is not caused by this PR.\n\n- The error: `the loop variable a is used to index dims` at `crates/gpu/src/cut.rs:126` (`clippy::needless_range_loop`), in `camcraft-gpu`.\n- `git diff origin/main...HEAD --stat` lists no file in `crates/gpu`.\n- The loop `for a in 0..3` is at the same line in `crates/gpu/src/cut.rs` on the merge base `60376ccbb` and on `origin/main` `f2b2369ed`. The file has no change between the two.\n- No open issue or PR tracks it. Issue #1624 is a closed case of the same lint in another crate. The open issue #3524 is a different red check on main.\n- The `camcraft-gcode` crate passes clippy with `-D warnings` alone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No caller uses the crate yet. The post round trip and the simulator are in the follow-up issues.\n- The controller presets (`fanuc`, `haas`, `tormach`, `grblhal`, `tinyg`, `carvera`) were not compared with a real controller.\n- A heavy lane is not required: the crate has no heavy test.\n\n## Unblocks\n\n#2218, #2219, #2222, #2227\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: Added the `camcraft-gcode` crate. It reads RS-274/NGC and ISO 6983 3-axis milling programs into toolpath sections with a 1-based line map, and refuses unsupported codes by name and line number.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #2217\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
